'''Michele Knotz''' is an American voice actress for the English dub of {{aniseries|PTS}} and {{aniseries|HZ}}.

==Biography==
Knotz was born sometime on October 27<!--Please do not edit this date. Michele Knotz has personally asked for her birth year not to be posted here--> in New Jersey and became a voice actress as an adult. She was the winner of the 2003 Anime Idol voice acting contest held at the now-defunct {{wp|Big Apple Anime Fest}} convention. The first runner-up, [[Hilary Thomas]], went on to provide voices for the {{TPCi}} dub before they became a producer for the show.

Knotz joined {{aniseries|PTS}} during the [[Pokémon USA recasting controversy]]. She debuted in ''[[The Mastermind of Mirage Pokémon]]'', where she played the roles of {{an|May}}, [[Jessie]], {{an|Misty}}, and [[Nurse Joy]]. She has since voiced several characters and Pokémon, but Jessie and May remain her most prominent roles. Notable Pokémon she voices include [[May's Beautifly]] and {{TP|May|Squirtle}} in {{aniseries|RS}}, [[Dawn's Piplup]] in {{aniseries|DP}}, [[Ash's Snivy]] and [[Jessie's Woobat]] in {{aniseries|BW}}, and the recurring {{an|Jigglypuff}} starting in {{aniseries|SM}}.

Aside from voice acting, Knotz does script adaptation for various dubs of foreign media. For the Pokémon franchise, she handled script adaptation for episodes 5-8 of [[Pokémon Concierge|''Pokémon Concierge'']] and the [[POKÉTOON]] episode [[PT19|''Another Day with Gardevoir'']].

